        "title": "I&quot;s",
        "raw_score": 6.475324758857977,
        "source": "kg"
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_9",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "The Kindaichi Case Files (Japanese: 金田一少年の事件簿 , Hepburn: Kindaichi Shōnen no Jikenbo ) is a Japanese mystery manga series based on the crime solving adventures of a high school student, Hajime Kindaichi, the supposed grandson of the famous (fictional) private detective Kosuke Kindaichi. They are written by Yōzaburō Kanari or Seimaru Amagi (depending on series) and illustrated by Fumiya Satō. The \"Kindaichi series\", which started serialization in \"Weekly Shōnen Magazine\" in 1992, is one of the earliest works in the mystery manga genre. In 1995, the manga won the Kodansha Manga Award for shōnen.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.05484838368846366,
      "temperature": 0.05484838368846366,
